"1007\"><strong data-start=\"917\" data-end=\"937\">Thermistor Type:</strong> 100K NTC (3950) precision sensor for accurate temperature detection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1008\" data-end=\"1092\">\n<p data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1092\"><strong data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1029\">Connector Type:</strong> Pre-crimped plug connector for quick and secure installation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1093\" data-end=\"1164\">\n<p data-start=\"1095\" data-end=\"1164\"><strong data-start=\"1095\" data-end=\"1116\">Cable Insulation:</strong> High-temperature PTFE and fiberglass sleeving</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1165\" data-end=\"1203\">\n<p data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1203\"><strong data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1189\">Temperature Range:</strong> Up to 300°C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1204\" data-end=\"1292\">\n<p data-start=\"1206\" data-end=\"1292\"><strong data-start=\"1206\" data-end=\"1219\">Function:</strong> Provides rapid and uniform heating along with precise thermal feedback</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1294\" data-end=\"1311\"><strong data-start=\"1294\" data-end=\"1309\">Advantages:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1312\" data-end=\"1611\">\n<li data-start=\"1312\" data-end=\"1367\">\n<p data-start=\"1314\" data-end=\"1367\">Consistent temperature control for stable extrusion</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1368\" data-end=\"1420\">\n<p data-start=\"1370\" data-end=\"1420\">Fast heat-up time with efficient energy transfer</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1421\" data-end=\"1482\">\n<p data-start=\"1423\" data-end=\"1482\">Durable, long-lasting materials for extended service life</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1483\" data-end=\"1547\">\n<p data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1547\">Easy plug-and-play replacement for the Kobra 2 hotend system</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1611\">\n<p data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1611\">Ideal for maintenance, part replacement, or hotend upgrades</p>\n</li>\n</ul>","variantSecondaryImages":["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443932483-205180634.jpg","https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443932440-742333080.jpg"]},{"id":"3467913d-af27-47c1-99ed-cefa716926a0","mrp":42999,"sku":"anycubic-kobra-3-v2-combo-3d-printer","name":"Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo 3D Printer","slug":"anycubic-kobra-3-v2-combo-3d-printer","brand":"e8665147-633e-4b6d-b462-cbfdc6114665","stock":0,"images":[{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false},{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933901-61875117.jpg","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false},{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933887-134314735.jpg","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false},{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933954-347014363.jpg","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false},{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443935819-511275858.jpg","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false}],"rating":4.5,"variants":[{"id":"445adb42-3431-485a-b0cd-4832a969ea25","sku":"anycubic-kobra-3-v2-combo-3d-printer-Default Title","name":"Default Title","price":"42999","stock":0,"images":[{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false}],"weight":"25000","isActive":true,"createdAt":"2026-07-19T06:57:07.418Z","deletedAt":null,"isDefault":false,"productId":"3467913d-af27-47c1-99ed-cefa716926a0","salePrice":null,"updatedAt":"2026-07-19T06:57:07.418Z","variantSlug":null,"optionValues":{"Title":"Default Title"},"primaryImage":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","galleryImages":["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png"],"variantImages":[{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","isPrimary":false,"sortOrder":0,"isSecondary":false}],"secondaryImage":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png"}],"salePrice":42999,"thumbnail":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","isFeatured":false,"category_id":"818c760a-e5d6-42fa-a68d-78bf45f3659d","dealerPrice":42999,"description":"<h2 data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"254\">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"645\">The Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo is a high-speed, multi-colour capable FDM printer with a large build volume, designed for users wanting quicker prints, colour/multi-material options, and a lot of smart features. The “Combo” refers to the fact that it includes the <strong data-start=\"516\" data-end=\"527\">ACE Pro</strong> module(s) that allow multi-colour/multi-filament printing (4-color, up to 8-color if two ACE Pros are used + the hub).<br></p>\n<h2 data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"231\">Product Description</h2>\n<p data-start=\"233\" data-end=\"450\">A high-performance, feature-rich FDM 3D printer designed for speed, multi-colour capability, and versatile material use. Built for serious prototyping, creative design, and flexible, high throughput printing workflows.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"455\">\n<h2 data-start=\"457\" data-end=\"499\">Key Features &amp; Technical Specifications</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<li data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"625\">\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"625\"><strong data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"519\">Build Volume</strong>: Approx. 255 × 255 × 260 mm — allows printing moderately large objects in one go without splitting parts.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"627\" data-end=\"828\">\n<p data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"662\"><strong data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"659\">Print Speed &amp; Acceleration</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"828\">\n<li data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"706\">\n<p data-start=\"667\" data-end=\"706\">Maximum travel speeds up to ~600 mm/s</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"745\">\n<p data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"745\">Acceleration up to ~20,000 mm/s²</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"748\" data-end=\"828\">\n<p data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"828\">Recommended operational speed lower (for best surface quality and reliability)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<p data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"854\"><strong data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"851\">Nozzle &amp; Hotend</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<li data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"957\">\n<p data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"957\">Standard nozzle diameter: 0.40 mm, with options for 0.60 mm or 0.80 mm to trade detail vs. speed</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<p data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"1050\">Maximum hotend temperature: ~300 °C, allowing use of more advanced engineering filaments</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<p data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1072\"><strong data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1069\">Build Plate</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<li data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1128\">\n<p data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1128\">Heated bed with maximum temperature up to ~110 °C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1131\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<p data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1236\">Flexible or spring-steel plate with PEI (or equivalent) surface for good adhesion and easy part release</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1238\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<p data-start=\"1240\" data-end=\"1286\"><strong data-start=\"1240\" data-end=\"1283\">Multi-colour / Multi-filament Capability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<li data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1383\">\n<p data-start=\"1291\" data-end=\"1383\">Enables printing with multiple filaments / colours via one or more filament-feeding modules</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<p data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1468\">Supports a setup with additional filament ports or hubs to manage several spools</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<p data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1505\"><strong data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1502\">Filament Handling &amp; Drying</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<li data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1637\">\n<p data-start=\"1510\" data-end=\"1637\">Built-in filament drying chamber or system maintained at moderate elevated temperature (≈ 35-55 °C) to reduce moisture issues</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1640\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<p data-start=\"1642\" data-end=\"1712\">Filament run-out detection and retraction or pause-on-run-out features</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1714\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<p data-start=\"1716\" data-end=\"1754\"><strong data-start=\"1716\" data-end=\"1751\">Auto-leveling &amp; Frame Stability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<li data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1820\">\n<p data-start=\"1759\" data-end=\"1820\">Automatic bed leveling system, reducing manual intervention</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"1926\">\n<p data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1926\">Reinforced frame / upgraded bearings on critical axes to minimize vibration/artifact at high speeds</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1929\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<p data-start=\"1931\" data-end=\"2006\">Wider gantry or support in one or more axes to improve leveling consistency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<p data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2035\"><strong data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2032\">Electrical &amp; Power</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<li data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2130\">\n<p data-start=\"2040\" data-end=\"2130\">Single power input unit, combined printer + module draw possibly up to ~400 W under load</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2133\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<p data-start=\"2135\" data-end=\"2221\">Compatible with typical mains supplies; ensure stable voltage and adequate ventilation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<p data-start=\"2225\" data-end=\"2259\"><strong data-start=\"2225\" data-end=\"2256\">User Interface &amp; Monitoring</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2262\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<li data-start=\"2262\" data-end=\"2368\">\n<p data-start=\"2264\" data-end=\"2368\">Touchscreen control panel (≈ 4-5 inch capacitive display) for job setup, adjustments, firmware updates</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2371\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<p data-start=\"2373\" data-end=\"2468\">Integrated camera for print monitoring; potential for remote status viewing, time-lapse capture</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<p data-start=\"2472\" data-end=\"2505\"><strong data-start=\"2472\" data-end=\"2502\">Safety &amp; Recovery Features</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2508\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<li data-start=\"2508\" data-end=\"2577\">\n<p data-start=\"2510\" data-end=\"2577\">Power-loss recovery (pauses print and resumes once power resumes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2580\" data-end=\"2641\">\n<p data-start=\"2582\" data-end=\"2641\">Detection of filament issues (run-out, jam, entanglement)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2644\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<p data-start=\"2646\" data-end=\"2688\">Temperature protections for hotend / bed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2690\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<p data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2718\"><strong data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2715\">Supported Filaments</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2721\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<li data-start=\"2721\" data-end=\"2779\">\n<p data-start=\"2723\" data-end=\"2779\">Standard materials: PLA, PETG, TPU (flexible filament)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2782\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<p data-start=\"2784\" data-end=\"2899\">With upgrade modules: ABS, ASA, PC, PA, PP, HIPS, etc. (depending on hotend grade, enclosure or ambient conditions)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2901\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<p data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2924\"><strong data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2921\">Nozzle Options</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2927\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<li data-start=\"2927\" data-end=\"2971\">\n<p data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2971\">Standard fine nozzle (0.4 mm) for detail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2974\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<p data-start=\"2976\" data-end=\"3050\">Larger nozzles (0.6-0.8 mm) for faster printing and larger layer heights</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3052\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<p data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3085\"><strong data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3082\">Physical Characteristics</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"3088\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<li data-start=\"3088\" data-end=\"3165\">\n<p data-start=\"3090\" data-end=\"3165\">Moderate footprint; heavy components if multi-filament module(s) attached</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3168\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<p data-start=\"3170\" data-end=\"3288\">Packaging includes printer base, filament feeding module(s), spool hub(es), power supply, build plate, and accessories</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start=\"3290\" data-end=\"3293\">\n<h2 data-start=\"3295\" data-end=\"3339\">Typical Operation Conditions &amp; Trade-Offs</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3962\">\n<li data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3471\">\n<p data-start=\"3343\" data-end=\"3471\">To maintain high print quality, speed, and accuracy, regular calibration is needed (bed leveling, checking belt tensions, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3473\" data-end=\"3634\">\n<p data-start=\"3475\" data-end=\"3634\">Fast printing tends to introduce artifacts like ringing or ghosting, especially on tall or detailed prints; slower speeds may be used when detail is important.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3636\" data-end=\"3769\">\n<p data-start=\"3638\" data-end=\"3769\">Multi-filament / colour printing increases complexity: oozing, colour bleed, nozzle purging, and filament transitions require tuning.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3771\" data-end=\"3962\">\n<p data-start=\"3773\" data-end=\"3962\">Environmental conditions (temperature, humidity, ventilation) play a significant role, particularly when printing materials sensitive to moisture or cooling quickly (ABS, ASA, Nylon, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"645\"><br><br></p>","isExclusive":false,"reviewCount":12,"codAvailable":true,"primaryImage":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","galleryImages":["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png","https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933901-61875117.jpg","https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933887-134314735.jpg","https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933954-347014363.jpg","https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443935819-511275858.jpg"],"variantImages":["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png"],"secondaryImage":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933901-61875117.jpg","shortDescription":"<h2 data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"254\">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"645\">The Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo is a high-speed, multi-colour capable FDM printer with a large build volume, designed for users wanting quicker prints, colour/multi-material options, and a lot of smart features. The “Combo” refers to the fact that it includes the <strong data-start=\"516\" data-end=\"527\">ACE Pro</strong> module(s) that allow multi-colour/multi-filament printing (4-color, up to 8-color if two ACE Pros are used + the hub).<br></p>\n<h2 data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"231\">Product Description</h2>\n<p data-start=\"233\" data-end=\"450\">A high-performance, feature-rich FDM 3D printer designed for speed, multi-colour capability, and versatile material use. Built for serious prototyping, creative design, and flexible, high throughput printing workflows.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"455\">\n<h2 data-start=\"457\" data-end=\"499\">Key Features &amp; Technical Specifications</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<li data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"625\">\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"625\"><strong data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"519\">Build Volume</strong>: Approx. 255 × 255 × 260 mm — allows printing moderately large objects in one go without splitting parts.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"627\" data-end=\"828\">\n<p data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"662\"><strong data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"659\">Print Speed &amp; Acceleration</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"828\">\n<li data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"706\">\n<p data-start=\"667\" data-end=\"706\">Maximum travel speeds up to ~600 mm/s</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"745\">\n<p data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"745\">Acceleration up to ~20,000 mm/s²</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"748\" data-end=\"828\">\n<p data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"828\">Recommended operational speed lower (for best surface quality and reliability)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<p data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"854\"><strong data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"851\">Nozzle &amp; Hotend</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<li data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"957\">\n<p data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"957\">Standard nozzle diameter: 0.40 mm, with options for 0.60 mm or 0.80 mm to trade detail vs. speed</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<p data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"1050\">Maximum hotend temperature: ~300 °C, allowing use of more advanced engineering filaments</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<p data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1072\"><strong data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1069\">Build Plate</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<li data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1128\">\n<p data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1128\">Heated bed with maximum temperature up to ~110 °C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1131\" data-end=\"1236\">\n<p data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1236\">Flexible or spring-steel plate with PEI (or equivalent) surface for good adhesion and easy part release</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1238\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<p data-start=\"1240\" data-end=\"1286\"><strong data-start=\"1240\" data-end=\"1283\">Multi-colour / Multi-filament Capability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<li data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1383\">\n<p data-start=\"1291\" data-end=\"1383\">Enables printing with multiple filaments / colours via one or more filament-feeding modules</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1468\">\n<p data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1468\">Supports a setup with additional filament ports or hubs to manage several spools</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<p data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1505\"><strong data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1502\">Filament Handling &amp; Drying</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<li data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1637\">\n<p data-start=\"1510\" data-end=\"1637\">Built-in filament drying chamber or system maintained at moderate elevated temperature (≈ 35-55 °C) to reduce moisture issues</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1640\" data-end=\"1712\">\n<p data-start=\"1642\" data-end=\"1712\">Filament run-out detection and retraction or pause-on-run-out features</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1714\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<p data-start=\"1716\" data-end=\"1754\"><strong data-start=\"1716\" data-end=\"1751\">Auto-leveling &amp; Frame Stability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<li data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1820\">\n<p data-start=\"1759\" data-end=\"1820\">Automatic bed leveling system, reducing manual intervention</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"1926\">\n<p data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1926\">Reinforced frame / upgraded bearings on critical axes to minimize vibration/artifact at high speeds</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1929\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<p data-start=\"1931\" data-end=\"2006\">Wider gantry or support in one or more axes to improve leveling consistency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<p data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2035\"><strong data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2032\">Electrical &amp; Power</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<li data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2130\">\n<p data-start=\"2040\" data-end=\"2130\">Single power input unit, combined printer + module draw possibly up to ~400 W under load</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2133\" data-end=\"2221\">\n<p data-start=\"2135\" data-end=\"2221\">Compatible with typical mains supplies; ensure stable voltage and adequate ventilation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<p data-start=\"2225\" data-end=\"2259\"><strong data-start=\"2225\" data-end=\"2256\">User Interface &amp; Monitoring</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2262\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<li data-start=\"2262\" data-end=\"2368\">\n<p data-start=\"2264\" data-end=\"2368\">Touchscreen control panel (≈ 4-5 inch capacitive display) for job setup, adjustments, firmware updates</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2371\" data-end=\"2468\">\n<p data-start=\"2373\" data-end=\"2468\">Integrated camera for print monitoring; potential for remote status viewing, time-lapse capture</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<p data-start=\"2472\" data-end=\"2505\"><strong data-start=\"2472\" data-end=\"2502\">Safety &amp; Recovery Features</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2508\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<li data-start=\"2508\" data-end=\"2577\">\n<p data-start=\"2510\" data-end=\"2577\">Power-loss recovery (pauses print and resumes once power resumes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2580\" data-end=\"2641\">\n<p data-start=\"2582\" data-end=\"2641\">Detection of filament issues (run-out, jam, entanglement)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2644\" data-end=\"2688\">\n<p data-start=\"2646\" data-end=\"2688\">Temperature protections for hotend / bed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2690\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<p data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2718\"><strong data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2715\">Supported Filaments</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2721\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<li data-start=\"2721\" data-end=\"2779\">\n<p data-start=\"2723\" data-end=\"2779\">Standard materials: PLA, PETG, TPU (flexible filament)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2782\" data-end=\"2899\">\n<p data-start=\"2784\" data-end=\"2899\">With upgrade modules: ABS, ASA, PC, PA, PP, HIPS, etc. (depending on hotend grade, enclosure or ambient conditions)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2901\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<p data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2924\"><strong data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2921\">Nozzle Options</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2927\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<li data-start=\"2927\" data-end=\"2971\">\n<p data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2971\">Standard fine nozzle (0.4 mm) for detail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2974\" data-end=\"3050\">\n<p data-start=\"2976\" data-end=\"3050\">Larger nozzles (0.6-0.8 mm) for faster printing and larger layer heights</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3052\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<p data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3085\"><strong data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3082\">Physical Characteristics</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"3088\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<li data-start=\"3088\" data-end=\"3165\">\n<p data-start=\"3090\" data-end=\"3165\">Moderate footprint; heavy components if multi-filament module(s) attached</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3168\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<p data-start=\"3170\" data-end=\"3288\">Packaging includes printer base, filament feeding module(s), spool hub(es), power supply, build plate, and accessories</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start=\"3290\" data-end=\"3293\">\n<h2 data-start=\"3295\" data-end=\"3339\">Typical Operation Conditions &amp; Trade-Offs</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3962\">\n<li data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3471\">\n<p data-start=\"3343\" data-end=\"3471\">To maintain high print quality, speed, and accuracy, regular calibration is needed (bed leveling, checking belt tensions, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3473\" data-end=\"3634\">\n<p data-start=\"3475\" data-end=\"3634\">Fast printing tends to introduce artifacts like ringing or ghosting, especially on tall or detailed prints; slower speeds may be used when detail is important.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3636\" data-end=\"3769\">\n<p data-start=\"3638\" data-end=\"3769\">Multi-filament / colour printing increases complexity: oozing, colour bleed, nozzle purging, and filament transitions require tuning.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3771\" data-end=\"3962\">\n<p data-start=\"3773\" data-end=\"3962\">Environmental conditions (temperature, humidity, ventilation) play a significant role, particularly when printing materials sensitive to moisture or cooling quickly (ABS, ASA, Nylon, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"645\"><br><br></p>","variantSecondaryImages":["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png"]},{"id":"44eef423-2598-47ca-9371-6c94dec0e9e5","mrp":899,"sku