ures for extended periods. The CR-10 heating block is designed to work with a variety of different filaments, including PLA, ABS, PETG, and TPU, and is often compatible with a range of different nozzle sizes to accommodate different printing requirements.</p>\n<p>It's important to note that heating blocks can wear out over time due to high-temperature cycling, so it's important to regularly inspect and replace the heating block to ensure optimal performance and printing quality.</p>","shortDescription":"<p>The CR-10 heating block is an essential component of a 3D printer that is responsible for heating the filament to its melting point before extrusion. The heating block is typically made of high-quality aluminum alloy to ensure efficient heat transfer and maintain a stable temperature during the printing process.</p>\n<p>The CR-10 heating block typically consists of a hollow cavity designed to hold a heating element, such as a cartridge heater or a thermistor, which is used to monitor the temperature of the block. A nozzle is screwed into the bottom of the block, which is responsible for extruding the melted filament through its small opening.</p>\n<p>To ensure efficient printing, the heating block must be capable of reaching and maintaining high temperatures for extended periods. The CR-10 heating block is designed to work with a variety of different filaments, including PLA, ABS, PETG, and TPU, and is often compatible with a range of different nozzle sizes to accommodate different printing requirements.</p>\n<p>It's important to note that heating blocks can wear out over time due to high-temperature cycling, so it's important to regularly inspect and replace the heating block to ensure optimal performance and printing quality.</p>","mrp":149,"salePrice":149,"dealerPrice":149,"stock":77,"images":[{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784444055171-654232076.jpg","isPrimary":false,"isSecondary":false,"sortOrder":0},{"